# REQUIRES: python-api, hdf5
# The deterministic properties with the lanes of the host pair rows
# (D[host-pair-vector]): the shipped default of the deterministic mode takes
# lanes(8) in f32 and lanes(4) in f64 on every host, while the suite pins
# MDIR_HOST_PAIRS=scalar, so the tests of these properties ran the scalar
# row. Here they run with MDIR_HOST_PAIRS unset, the default.
# A Python simulation against mdir run, in one part and in segments
# (Inputs/python_deterministic_run.py, as python-deterministic-run-*-pme.test).
#
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t/mixed %t/double
# RUN: env -u MDIR_HOST_PAIRS MDIR_COMPILE_CACHE_DIR=%t/cache %mdir_python %S/Inputs/python_deterministic_run.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide CPU mdir %t/mixed Mixed PME 1 21 20x3 7x5 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=MIXED
# RUN: env -u MDIR_HOST_PAIRS MDIR_COMPILE_CACHE_DIR=%t/cache %mdir_python %S/Inputs/python_deterministic_run.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide CPU mdir %t/double Double PME 1 21 20x3 7x5 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=DOUBLE

# MIXED: CPU Mixed PME 1: positions same velocities same forces same
# MIXED-NEXT: CPU Mixed PME 21: positions same velocities same forces same
# MIXED-NEXT: CPU Mixed PME 20x3: positions same velocities same forces same
# MIXED-NEXT: CPU Mixed PME 7x5: positions same velocities same forces same
# DOUBLE: CPU Double PME 1: positions same velocities same forces same
# DOUBLE-NEXT: CPU Double PME 21: positions same velocities same forces same
# DOUBLE-NEXT: CPU Double PME 20x3: positions same velocities same forces same
# DOUBLE-NEXT: CPU Double PME 7x5: positions same velocities same forces same
